!Sample_data_row_count = 0
^SAMPLE = GSM4796779
!Sample_title = ZM12 [sgNC-8-RFP + CC-122]
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM4796779
!Sample_status = Public on Oct 01 2020
!Sample_submission_date = Sep 21 2020
!Sample_last_update_date = Oct 01 2020
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = B lymphocyte
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: SU-DHL-4
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = SU-DHL-4 cells were transduced with a lentiviral vector expressing either sgNT-1 or sgNC-8 and then selected by puromycin (2µg/mL) for three days.  Cells were then spin down and resuspended with fresh medium and seeded in  6 well plates at one million cells per mL and treated with either DMSO or 10 µM CC-122 for 24 hours. Cells were washed once by ice cold PBS and then the cell pellets were snap frozen and kept at -80 °C. One cell pellet from each condition was subjected to western blot to check the CRISPR editing of target genes and Ikaros degradation.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = SU-DHL-4 was maintained in RPMI 1640 medium (RPMI; #11875085, Thermo Fisher) supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum, 1X sodium pyruvate, 1X non-essential amino acids, 100 U/mL penicillin, and 100 µg/mL streptomycin. When applicable, puromycin (#A1113803, Thermo Fisher), blasticidin (#A1113903, Thermo Fisher) or Hygromycin B (#10687010, Thermo Fisher) was added to the cell culture medium at 2 µg/ml, 10-50 µg/ml and 400 µg/ml respectively .Cells were cultured at 37 °C in a humidified 5% CO2 atmosphere.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Duplicates of about 1 million freshly frozen, pelleted cells for each condition were shipped to GENEWIZ (South Plainfield, NJ). The RNA extraction was performed using QIAGEN RNeasy Plus Mini Kit and the mRNA was enriched through poly-A+ mRNA.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The RNA extractio library preparation, and mRNAseq were performed by GENEWIZ using the NEBNext® Ultra™ II RNA Library Prep Kit for Illumina (#7765, New England Biolabs). ERCC RNA spike-in mix (#4456653, invitrogen) was spiked into each sample after RNA extraction and universal human reference RNA (#14919, Thermal fisher) was included for quality control purpose.
!Sample_data_processing = Raw fastq files were merged so that each sample had one R1 and one R2 files. The quality of the fastq files was evaluated using FastqQC (v 0.11.5). The fastq files were tested using bbmap reformat (v.37.24) for compliance with the fastq format and to convert the quality encoding to q33. Illumina adapters were trimmed using cutadapt (v1.15) and used for Salmon and any other downstream process.    In all analyses the primary assembly of hg38 was used (ENCODE version) and the annotation from Gencode v24. Alignment was performed using a two pass mode with STAR (v2.5.2b) on the full genome and counts were obtained using the quantmode GeneCounts option, STAR was also used to trim the reads on the fly using the clip3pAdapterSequence option. Salmon (v 0.7) was used to obtain pseudoalignments on genes on the trimmed fastq files.
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Salmon Raw Counts
