!Sample_data_processing = Raw fastq files were merged so that each sample had one R1 and one R2 files. The quality of the fastq files was evaluated using FastqQC (v 0.11.5). The fastq files were tested using bbmap reformat (v.37.24) for compliance with the fastq format and to convert the quality encoding to q33. Illumina adapters were trimmed using cutadapt (v1.15) and used for Salmon and any other downstream process.    In all analyses the primary assembly of hg38 was used (ENCODE version) and the annotation from Gencode v24. Alignment was performed using a two pass mode with STAR (v2.5.2b) on the full genome and counts were obtained using the quantmode GeneCounts option, STAR was also used to trim the reads on the fly using the clip3pAdapterSequence option. Salmon (v 0.7) was used to obtain pseudoalignments on genes on the trimmed fastq files.
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Salmon Raw Counts
!Sample_platform_id = GPL20301
!Sample_contact_name = Rajkumar,,Balakrishnan
!Sample_contact_email = rajkumar.balakrishnan@bms.com
!Sample_contact_laboratory = Knowledge Science Research
!Sample_contact_department = Informatics & Predictive Sciences
