^SAMPLE = GSM4888722
!Sample_title = ZM23 [sgCYLD-5-RFP + CC-122]
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM4888722
!Sample_status = Public on Nov 08 2020
!Sample_submission_date = Nov 07 2020
!Sample_last_update_date = Nov 08 2020
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = B lymphocyte
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: SU-DHL-4
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = SU-DHL-4 cells were transduced with a lentiviral vector expressing a sgRNA targeting either CYLD (sgCYLD-2, sgCYLD-5), NFKBIA (sgNFKBIA-5, sgNFKBIA-8 ), TRAF3 (sgTRAF3-4, sgTRAF3-7) or TRAF2 (sgTRAF2-3, sgTRAF2-4) and then selected by puromycin (2µg/mL) for three days.  Cells were then spin down and resuspended with fresh medium and seeded in 6 well plates at one million cells per mL and treated with either DMSO or 10 µM CC-122 for 24 hours. Cells were washed once by ice cold PBS and then the cell pellets were snap frozen and kept at -80 °C. One cell pellet from each condition was subjected to western blot to check the CRISPR editing of target genes and Ikaros degradation.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = SU-DHL-4 was maintained in RPMI 1640 medium (RPMI; #11875085, Thermo Fisher) supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum, 1X sodium pyruvate, 1X non-essential amino acids, 100 U/mL penicillin, and 100 µg/mL streptomycin. Cells were cultured at 37 °C in a humidified 5% CO2 atmosphere.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Duplicates of about 1 million freshly frozen, pelleted cells for each condition were shipped to GENEWIZ (South Plainfield, NJ). The RNA extraction was performed using QIAGEN RNeasy Plus Mini Kit and the mRNA was enriched through poly-A+ mRNA.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The RNA extraction, library preparation, and mRNAseq were performed by GENEWIZ using the NEBNext® Ultra™ II RNA Library Prep Kit for Illumina (#7765, New England Biolabs). ERCC RNA spike-in mix (#4456653, invitrogen) was spiked into each sample after RNA extraction and universal human reference RNA (#14919, Thermal fisher) was included for quality control purpose.
